Package: branchpilot
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libgtk-3-0, git (>= 2.28)
# git is a hard dependency rather than a Recommends: BranchPilot has no
# bundled git and no libgit2 — every operation shells out to the system
# binary, so without it the application cannot open a repository at all.
# The >= 2.28 floor is `git init --initial-branch`, which the app relies on
# and which predates every currently supported Ubuntu release.
#
# ssh-client is only a Suggests: HTTPS remotes with a credential helper are
# a complete workflow on their own, and a user who never touches SSH remotes
# should not be made to install it.
Suggests: ssh-client
Description: Git GUI with a visual commit graph and hunk-level staging
 BranchPilot is a git client for the Linux desktop: a visual commit graph,
 hunk-level staging, full branch, stash and remote operations, and a
 drag-and-drop editor for interactive rebase.
 .
 It wraps the system git command-line tool directly — there is no libgit2,
 no bundled git binary, and the application never handles or stores
 credentials. Authentication stays exactly where it already lives: your
 existing git credential helpers and ssh-agent.
 .
 Features include a commit graph with persistent lane assignment and
 colour-coded refs, syntax-highlighted diffs with per-hunk staging, branch
 and stash management, fetch, pull and push with live progress, interactive
 rebase with conflict resume, and power operations such as tags,
 cherry-pick, revert, reset, worktrees and per-file history.
